agents modified XHTTP packet-up transport

Protocol/design reference:
  XTLS/Xray-core, transport/internet/splithttp
  https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/tree/0f127f934c6d7c10e4bb6acbe98033db9e5fd922/transport/internet/splithttp
  Upstream license: Mozilla Public License 2.0 (see LICENSE in this directory).

Packet-up upload design (buffered coalescing writes, concurrent POSTs started
once the previous request is written, minimum POST interval, sequence-ordered
upload queue that drops stale packets and closes on an oversized backlog, and
the scMaxEachPostBytes/scMaxBufferedPosts/scMinPostsIntervalMs defaults):
  XTLS/Xray-core, transport/internet/splithttp/dialer.go and upload_queue.go
  https://github.com/XTLS/Xray-core/tree/7da5dae6502b787fc6d903863e9a6c5043d107a2/transport/internet/splithttp

This directory implements a rewritten, modified packet-up transport in Go's
standard library. It follows the upstream split HTTP idea (long GET download,
sequenced bounded POST upload and bounded reordering), with a different wire
format, mandatory per-request authorization and explicit connection lifecycle.
It does not import or embed Xray, VLESS, Reverse, or Xray Mux. It is not a claim
of wire compatibility with native Xray XHTTP configurations or all XHTTP modes.

